{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/485532-cryptid-revenants-fast-zombies","id":485532,"title":"Cryptid Revenants (fast zombies)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-19T12:01:41-07:00","id":485532,"title":"Cryptid Revenants (fast zombies)","content":"Both cryptid and revenant parts are probably partially irrelevant to the scenario.<br /> <br /> In my chronicle I've got an underground &quot;water treatment&quot; plant that is actually treating blood. It's god machine infrastructure that has been suborned by Belial's Brood. it always treated blood, but what great supply of food. It also has something to do with concealment infrastructure, and preventing people from seeing reality. It turns out that vitae increases the output of the plant (because in my head canon god machine feeds on essence which has something to do with the soul and vitae is stronger in it).<br /> <br /> The brood has been dropping it's corpses down there as well as studying the infrastructure, these corpses are coming back as revenants (maybe not all) but being &quot;embraced&quot; so close to infrastructure has changed them. It has enhanced their beast as well as making them hungry for Aether, currently they are living amidst the tanks of Aether polluted blood. When Demon's show up though, they'll look like a much tastier snack.<br /> <br /> The demon's show up and the linchpin is obvious, however the numerous cryptid vamps decide to make them a snack.<br /> <br /> what I'd like are suggestions on how I should change the vamps from normal to elaborate on them being cryptids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T14:48:34-07:00","id":485735,"title":"","content":"Id suggest mostly say use the base of revenant then the rules for a cryptid (rank 1). Adaptations I'd suggest are 1) aether eater and 2) aether storage with both replacing vitae. <br /> <br /> Though I'd suggest giving them something like an extreme brand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T21:21:51-07:00","id":486014,"title":"","content":"Okay, are you intending these to be vampiric cryptids, or actual vampire cryptids?<br /> <br /> Because if the first, then you can just use the normal cryptid rules and give it a vampire theme, if the second, then the cryptids would have all the traits and abilities of a vampire plus whatever cryptid abilities you give them, because cryptids don't actually lose any traits in the transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T04:25:12-07:00","id":486219,"title":"","content":"Total thread derailment, but this is the 666th topic in this forum. There can be no further topics, clearly. <br /> <br /> On topic... I'd approach this slightly differently. Cryptids look <i>different</i>, often with biomechanical or general supernatural changes to their original appearance. How do the cryptid-revenants appear? Do they have hypodermic needles on their fingers? Are they standardised or is each a unique-looking monster? I'd start with their appearance then make powers to fit. So, syringe-fingers is a fine claw analogue with Aether Eater built in. It also clearly physically demarks them from regular vampires when IV tubing protrudes from their skin, filling with blood when they feed, or their teeth are replaced with rusted metal fangs, their eyes replaced by giant screws or lenses.... Have fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}